<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS MODERN STATE OF DIAL UP BBSES</pattern>
<template>As of June 2026, approximately 1,046 BBSes are listed in the Telnet BBS Guide, indicating a small but active community of traditional dial-up BBSes.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS CURRENT STATUS OF MODERN TELNET BBSES</pattern>
<template>Modern telnet BBSes represent a niche but enduring legacy of the bulletin board system era. While the commercial BBS market collapsed in the mid-1990s due to internet competition, a small but active community persists, with most surviving BBSes still accessible via Telnet. The FidoNet network continues to operate with Telnet-based BBS connections, and a resurgence around 2014 brought renewed interest in internet-connected BBS.</template>
</category>
